<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bratislava</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pressburg, Pozsony</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bratislava is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovakia">Slovakia</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> near the borders with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>. A Celtic oppidum of the Boii stood there in the 1st century BCE. Known as Pressburg in German and Pozsony in Hungarian, it was the coronation city and seat of the diet of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a> from the 16th to the 19th centuries, and became capital of an independent Slovakia in 1993.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bratislava.jpg" alt="Bratislava" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arne Müseler · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Slovakia_bratislava.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
